# Vercel ignore — repo root.
#
# Background: the deploy script (web/scripts/deploy-prod.sh) runs vercel
# from the repo root because the Vercel project's Root Directory setting
# is `web/` (running vercel from web/ would resolve to <repo>/web/web/).
# Without this ignore, vercel uploads the entire repo — including data/
# (multi-GB cached PDFs), supabase/, src/, etc. — and Vercel rejects
# deploys whose source tree exceeds 15000 files OR several GB.
#
# Vercel's Root Directory project setting still controls what becomes the
# build context. This ignore just keeps non-web/ paths out of the upload
# in the first place so we don't hit upload limits.
#
# .vercelignore uses gitignore syntax. We can't use the simple "ignore *
# then re-allow web/" pattern because Vercel's parser doesn't always
# honor the unignore-re-include reliably across nested paths. List
# everything we DON'T want to upload explicitly.

# Backend Python pipeline + tests + data
src/
tests/
data/
mcp/
scripts/

# Database migrations + Supabase CLI state
supabase/
*.sql

# Internal docs (not needed for the build)
docs/
*.md
LICENSE

# Claude worktrees, AI artifacts, local state
.claude/
.sfdx/
tmp/
JOURNAL.md
*.log

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Node artifacts outside web/ (web/ has its own ignores via .gitignore)
node_modules/

# Repo-wide test/CI config not needed at deploy time
pytest.ini
requirements*.txt

# Vercel itself
.vercel/
